/*
 * Beak: MatTooltip has no arrow of its own (confirmed against the compiled
 * template — just the surface `<div>`, nothing else), so it's a rotated
 * square `::after` on the outer `.mat-mdc-tooltip` div (which Material
 * leaves free — it only uses `::before` there, for its own invisible
 * hit-area extension) rather than on `.mat-mdc-tooltip-surface` itself
 * (which has `overflow: hidden` in Material's own CSS and would clip
 * anything positioned outside its bounds).
 *
 * Orientation comes from the CDK overlay panel's own position class
 * (`.mat-mdc-tooltip-panel-{above,below,left,right}`, applied by Material
 * to an ancestor of `.mat-mdc-tooltip` — confirmed the same way Material's
 * own `::before` hit-area rule keys off it) — points toward whichever edge
 * is closest to the trigger.
