 * their own template (`<ng-template cdkConnectedOverlay>`), so they can
 * stamp a custom marker class (`.rec-dropdown-panel`, etc.) directly onto
 * it — every selector in their overlay CSS is scoped under that marker,
 * gated by `[data-recursica-theme]`, so a plain non-Recursica CDK overlay
 * elsewhere is never touched. `MatDatepickerContent` offers no equivalent
 * hook: I don't own its template, and `MatDatepicker.panelClass` only
 * reaches `<mat-calendar>` itself, not the `mat-datepicker-content` host
 * (confirmed by reading `MatDatepickerContent`'s compiled template).
