 *     narrower-than-usual limitation of this one component, not a bug.
 *
 * Range-selection states (`data-in-range`/`data-comparison-*`/`data-preview-*`)
 * are intentionally not styled — matching the reference's own scope limit
 * (`RecursicaDatePickerProps` doesn't discriminate on `type`, so range mode
 * isn't reachable through the public API on either adapter; see
 * DATEPICKER_IMPLEMENTATION_NOTES.md §3 in the genesis reference).
 *
 * "Outside month" day dimming (present in the Mantine reference) has no
 * Angular equivalent to style: `MatMonthView` only renders the current
 * month's real day cells, filling the leading/trailing offset with blank
 * label cells, not dimmed adjacent-month day numbers — a real, structural
 * difference from Mantine's calendar, not a simplification made here.
