 * `width: 100%` — required because `AutoCompleteControlComponent` already
 * binds `[cdkConnectedOverlayWidth]="overlayWidth"` (the trigger's own
 * `offsetWidth`, captured on open) onto CDK's `.cdk-overlay-pane` wrapper —
 * confirmed live that binding *does* correctly set `.cdk-overlay-pane`'s
 * inline `width`. But `.cdk-overlay-pane` is itself `display: flex` (CDK's
 * own default, row-direction), and without `width: 100%` here this panel —
 * a flex *item* along that row's main axis — sized to its own content
 * (`flex-grow: 0` default) instead of stretching to fill the pane, so a
 * short-labeled option list (e.g. "Alpha"/"Beta"/...) rendered a panel far
 * narrower than the trigger, confirmed live via Playwright (pane measured
 * 320px, this panel measured ~82px) — not a missing panel-width *binding*
 * (already wired), a missing *fill* rule on the bound width's target.
 */
[data-recursica-theme] .rec-autocomplete-panel {
  width: 100%;
  overflow: auto;
  max-height: 320px;
  box-sizing: border-box;
